WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.260
- There's been a lot of buzz

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:03.090
about how the diabetes drug metformin,

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.440
could help people live longer.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.020
Results are mixed on
metformin's actual efficacy

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.340
as an anti aging treatment.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.770
One way metformin is supposed
to help with anti aging

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.980
is by activating a cellular
process called autophagy.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.900
It literally means self eating.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.610
Your cells do this all the time

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:19.680
to keep themselves and you healthy.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.040
Let's go over how autophagy
works and its role in aging.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.800
Think of autophagy as your
cells recycling system.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.080
Cells use autophagy to get rid of proteins

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.460
and other cellular components

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.400
that aren't working properly
or could cause problems.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.010
This process goes a little
something like this.

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:36.810
Little sacks engulf proteins

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:40.140
in structures like mitochondria,
the powerhouses of cells.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.960
These sacks infuse with
another cellular compartment

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.490
called the lysosome.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.320
Think of it as a cell shredder.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.120
The sack's cargo gets broken down there

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.653
by enzymes in the lysosome.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.760
And cells can then reuse these
materials to build new stuff.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:55.320
That makes autophagy protective

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:57.690
against aging and stress in two ways.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.840
It provides cells with energy,
especially when food is low

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:02.820
and it prevents junk from piling up.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:05.490
But as we age, autophagy levels go down

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.230
and the damage our bodies accumulate

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.720
at the cellular level goes up.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.090
Longevity experts think the damage buildup

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.310
is one of the main reasons we age.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:16.620
Damage can happen even
from basic functions

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:18.720
like breathing and metabolizing food,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.700
kind of like when we
burn fuel in our cars.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.220
These reactions can
produce tiny pollutants

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.570
that can cause inflamation

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:26.640
and harm proteins in mitochondria.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.000
Over time there's too much
damage or not enough repair

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.400
and cells just don't work as
well as when they were younger,

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.680
in worst case scenario, they die.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.590
That's why certain diseases
become more common with age.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.530
For diabetes impaired
autophagy is associated

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.230
with insulin resistance,
a hallmark of a disease,

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.910
and in some types of dementia,

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:46.830
brain cells that can't
get rid of protein clumps

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.900
through autophagy, they die.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.280
By promoting autophagy,

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.200
the goal is to increase health span

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.750
or the amount of time we
can live a healthy life

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.540
free of debilitating
age related conditions

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.310
like dementia and diabetes.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.920
And if lifespan is extended
too, all the better.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.110
Since metformin helps increase autophagy

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.960
that might mean it also
helps prevent cellular damage

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:07.890
and therefore aging.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.920
There are other drugs and
methods that can boost autophagy.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:12.780
Resveratrol is an anti-tumor drug

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:15.120
that's also a powerful antioxidant.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.220
And rapamycin is an immunosuppressant

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:20.130
that's been shown to
extend lifespan in animals,

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.480
kind of like metformin.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.700
Some longevity experts are also looking at

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.320
intermittent fasting.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.060
There's already preliminary evidence

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.440
that it promotes brain health.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.660
When you don't eat, autophagy increases

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.920
to fill the energy void.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.560
In mice, research suggests
that increased autophagy

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.880
allows them to live longer

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:38.040
and their organs to age less quickly

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.350
but that doesn't always
translate to humans.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.870
Sometimes, doses that are
used in animal studies

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.840
are way higher than what
people can take safely.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.600
Plus taking any medication
has side effects.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.060
For metformin, those include a higher risk

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.510
of Parkinson's disease and
difficulty building muscle mass,

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.730
potentially because of too much autophagy.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.050
And in transplant patients,

00:02:58.050 --> 00:03:00.150
who take rapamycin more frequently

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:02.880
and at higher doses than
longevity bio-hackers,

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.460
common side effects can
include mouth ulcers,

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.110
loss of kidney function

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.960
and high blood pressure and
high cholesterol levels.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.550
Understanding how people age

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.620
and why some people age better than others

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.440
could help us develop
better anti-aging therapies,

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.640
and that's critical,

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:20.877
given the world's
population is aging fast.

00:03:20.877 --> 00:03:23.460
(upbeat music)

